Chapter: GroundsPort
  grounds Device.Port

 A chapter that grounds Device.Port may perform port I/O in its bodies
 without declaring the effect -- the internal exemption of BACKLOG 1.8,
 declared in the file instead of the compiler's hardcoded quire list.
 touch performs port-out-byte (a [Device.Port] intrinsic) while its own
 signature is pure and it is not in an exempt quire; without the grounds
 line this is CDX2031. The effectful let is legal here for the same
 reason -- a grounding chapter's bodies need no act-conversion.

Section: Body
  touch : Integer -> Integer
  touch (p) =
   let w = port-out-byte p 0
   in w

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let r = touch 128
   in print-line-uni "grounded"
  end
